# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in the working
# tree while files written by tooling stay LF, so the same commit behaves
# differently on two machines. That is not hypothetical: it broke
# scripts/check-db-imports.mjs, which split on "\n" and was left a trailing \r
# that stopped its comment-stripping regexes matching -- the tenant-isolation
# lint failed on a fresh clone while passing on the machine that wrote the code.
#
# eol=lf rather than eol=native: this repo has SQL migrations and shell-ish
# scripts that are read by tools, not just by editors, and one line-ending
# convention everywhere is the only version that is reproducible.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
